# Monero Wallet CLI Automation with Expect

Non-interactive wallet generation/restoration using `expect`. Requires `sudo apt install -y expect`.

## Generate New Wallet

```expect
#!/usr/bin/expect -f
set timeout 120
spawn /tmp/monero-x86_64-linux-gnu-v*/monero-wallet-cli \
    --generate-new-wallet=/tmp/monero-wallet \
    --password-file=/tmp/pw.txt \
    --log-level=0

expect "language of your choice:" { send "1\r" }
expect eof
```

The seed phrase is printed after wallet creation. Capture it:
```bash
grep -A2 "can be used to recover" /tmp/monero-x86_64-linux-gnu-v*/monero-wallet-cli.log
```

## Restore from Seed

```expect
#!/usr/bin/expect -f
set timeout 120
spawn /tmp/monero-x86_64-linux-gnu-v*/monero-wallet-cli \
    --restore-deterministic-wallet \
    --generate-new-wallet=/tmp/restored-wallet \
    --password-file=/tmp/pw.txt \
    --daemon-address=stagenet.melo.tools:38081 \
    --daemon-ssl disabled \
    --log-level=0

expect "language of your choice:" { send "1\r" }
expect "Enter your seed" { send "your seed phrase here\r" }
expect "new password" { send "walletpass\r" }
expect "password again" { send "walletpass\r" }
expect eof
```

## Key Points

- `--password-file` skips password prompt (create with `echo -n 'mypass' > /tmp/pw.txt`)
- `--daemon-address` is optional for creation (can sync later)
- `--log-level=0` suppresses verbose output
- The `expect "language of your choice:"` pattern must be exact — match the full prompt text
- The Monero CLI takes ~8-10 seconds to start Tor, so `timeout 120` is needed
- After successful creation, wallet files are: `wallet`, `wallet.keys`, `wallet.address`

## Verifying the Wordlist

The English wordlist is embedded in the monero-wallet-cli binary. To verify seed words:

```bash
strings /path/to/monero-wallet-cli | grep "^${word}$"
```

The wordlist starts with "abbey" and contains exactly 1626 English words.
